      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles. Two triangles are similar if their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are proportional. \n\nGiven:\n- The side lengths of the original isosceles triangle are 8 cm, 8 cm, and 10 cm.\n- The longest side of the similar triangle is 25 cm.\n\nSince the triangles are similar, the ratio of the corresponding sides will be the same. The longest side of the original triangle is 10 cm, and the longest side of the similar triangle is 25 cm. \n\nTo find the scale factor, we divide the longest side of the similar triangle by the longest side of the original triangle:\n\\[\n\\text{Scale factor} = \\frac{25 \\text{ cm}}{10 \\text{ cm}} = 2.5\n\\]\n\nNow, we use this scale factor to find the lengths of the other sides of the similar triangle. The original triangle has sides 8 cm, 8 cm, and 10 cm. Applying the scale factor of 2.5 to each side, we get:\n\\[\n\\text{New side lengths} = 8 \\text{ cm} \\times 2.5 = 20 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{New side lengths} = 8 \\text{ cm} \\times 2.5 = 20 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{New side lengths} = 10 \\text{ cm} \\times 2.5 = 25 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nSo, the side lengths of the similar triangle are 20 cm, 20 cm, and 25 cm.\n\nTo find the perimeter of the similar triangle, we add up all its side lengths:\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter} = 20 \\text{ cm} + 20 \\text{ cm} + 25 \\text{ cm} = 65 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of the larger triangle is \\boxed{65} centimeters.",
